.\" @(#)mcpserver.1  0.3.0  2026
.TH mcpserver 1 "2026" "mcpserver-irix 0.3.0" "IRIX User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcpserver \- operator CLI and stdio bridge for the IRIX MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcpserver
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcpserver
is the operator interface to
.BR mcpserverd (1M),
the IRIX MCP server daemon.
It provides subcommands to manage the daemon lifecycle, edit the project
registry, generate and apply policy, and run the MCP stdio bridge.
.PP
The
.B stdio
subcommand is the primary integration point for AI clients.
When invoked over an SSH session,
.B "mcpserver stdio"
speaks MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin/stdout and proxies requests to the
local
.B mcpserverd
socket.
Diagnostics go to stderr only; stdout is reserved for MCP traffic.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Daemon management
.TP
.B start
Start
.BR mcpserverd .
.TP
.B stop
Stop
.BR mcpserverd .
.TP
.B restart
Stop, then start
.BR mcpserverd .
.TP
.B status
Print boot enable state (from
.BR chkconfig )
and current daemon PID, or
.I stopped
if the daemon is not running.
.TP
.B enable
Mark the daemon to start at boot
.RB ( chkconfig " flag on)"
and start it immediately.
.TP
.B disable
Stop the daemon and mark it not to start at boot.
.TP
.B logs " [" N ]
Print the last
.I N
lines of syslog output from
.BR mcpserverd .
Default is 80 lines.
.SS Configuration management
.TP
.B show
Print the current project registry
.RI ( /etc/mcpserver/projects.json )
in tabular form, one project per line with name, access mode, and root path.
.TP
.BI "add " "name root " "--rw" | "--ro" " [--deny " pattern "...]"
Add a project entry to the registry.
.I name
is a short identifier.
.I root
must be an absolute path.
.B --rw
grants read-write access;
.B --ro
grants read-only access.
Repeat
.B --deny
to add glob patterns that block access to matching paths within the root.
Deny patterns must be relative and must not contain
.BR .. .
Writes to
.I /etc/mcpserver/projects.json
immediately; run
.B mcpserver apply
to activate the change in the daemon.
.TP
.BI "remove " name
Remove the named project from the registry.
Writes to
.I /etc/mcpserver/projects.json
immediately; run
.B mcpserver apply
to activate.
.TP
.B validate
Validate the project registry and the policy that would be generated
from it.
Checks for duplicate names, duplicate roots, absolute deny patterns,
and
.B ..
in deny patterns.
Then generates the policy and attempts to load it.
Exits 0 on success, 1 on any error.
.TP
.B preview
Print to stdout the
.I boundaries.json
that
.B mcpserver apply
would write, without modifying anything.
Useful for reviewing a proposed policy change.
.TP
.B apply
Generate
.I /etc/mcpserver/boundaries.json
from the current project registry.
The previous
.I boundaries.json
is backed up to
.IR /etc/mcpserver/backup/ .
If the daemon is running,
.B SIGHUP
is sent so it reloads the new policy without a restart.
.SS Bridge mode
.TP
.B stdio
Connect to the running
.B mcpserverd
and run as a MCP stdio bridge.
Reads JSON-RPC 2.0 requests from stdin, forwards them to the daemon
over
.IR /var/run/mcpserverd.sock ,
and writes responses to stdout.
Exits when stdin is closed.
This is the mode invoked by Claude Code and Codex via SSH; it should
not be run interactively.
.SS Miscellaneous
.TP
.B help
Print a usage summary.
.TP
.B version
Print the version string.
.SH WORKFLOW
Typical workflow for adding a new project:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mcpserver add myproj /usr/people/me/src --rw
mcpserver validate
mcpserver preview
mcpserver apply
.fi
.RE
.PP
The
.B apply
step signals the running daemon; no restart is required.
.PP
To connect Claude Code to the IRIX machine, configure the MCP server
entry in Claude Code to run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ssh root@\fIhostname\fP mcpserver stdio
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mcpserver/projects.json
Operator project registry.
Managed by
.B mcpserver add
and
.BR "mcpserver remove" .
.TP
.I /etc/mcpserver/boundaries.json
Active policy file loaded by
.BR mcpserverd (1M).
Written by
.BR "mcpserver apply" .
.TP
.I /etc/mcpserver/backup/
Backups of previous
.I boundaries.json
files, named with a timestamp suffix.
.TP
.I /var/run/mcpserverd.pid
Daemon PID file; read by status, stop, restart, and apply.
.TP
.I /var/run/mcpserverd.sock
UNIX-domain socket connecting the bridge to the daemon.
.TP
.I /var/config/mcpserver
.BR chkconfig (1M)
flag file managed by
.B enable
and
.BR disable .
.TP
.I /etc/init.d/mcpserverd
Init script invoked by boot sequences and by
.B start
and
.BR stop .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
An error occurred; a message is printed to stderr.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR mcpserverd (1M),
.BR chkconfig (1M),
.BR syslog (3)
.SH NOTES
Daemon management subcommands
.RB ( start ,
.BR stop ,
.BR restart ,
.BR enable ,
.BR disable ,
.BR apply )
require root privileges.
.PP
.B "mcpserver stdio"
must be run as root or as the owner of
.I /var/run/mcpserverd.sock
in order to connect to the daemon.
.PP
This program is part of the
.B mcpserver-irix
package, version 0.3.0.
